==============================================================================
O27 — joint dyadic/triadic prime difference table  (EXPLORATORY: no prereg, no verdict)
==============================================================================
  N_b(r)   = pi(b^r) - pi(b^(r-1))        primes in (b^(r-1), b^r]
  T_b(r,d) = T_b(r,d-1) - T_b(r-1,d-1)    backward, support r = d+1..R
  FIRST BLOCK: pi(1) = 0 (1 is neither prime nor composite). Block r covers the half-open interval (b^(r-1), b^r], so block 1 is (1, b] and excludes 1. Hence N_2(1) = pi(2) = 1 and N_3(1) = pi(3) = 2.
  PAIRING: by ROW INDEX r, not by magnitude. Dyadic r=10 (x=1024) sits on the
  same row as triadic r=10 (x=59049). Intentional — do not align on x.
  BLANKS: a cell with r < d+1 does not exist and is emitted BLANK, never 0.
  ARITHMETIC: exact Python int throughout. numpy is deliberately NOT imported.

